# Line endings, pinned where they matter.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, but the
# files below are read by Linux, not by Windows:
#
#   * deploy/backup.sh is bind-mounted straight into the backup
#     container and run by dash. A CRLF `set -eu` is a hard error there,
#     so a git checkout that rewrote the line endings would crash-loop
#     the container on the documented `docker compose up` path.
#   * Dockerfiles with `\` continuations: the CRLF rides along on the
#     continued line and the instruction is mangled — builds break in a
#     way that reads as a typo.
#   * The Caddyfile is parsed by a Linux process for the same reason.
#
# `eol=lf` on both sides means the working copy is always LF as well, so
# what runs locally is what runs on the server.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
